Source: zyphor-os-settings-gnome
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Mark Jason Espelita <markjasonespelita@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: zyphor-os-settings-gnome
Architecture: all
# What the settings name: the schemas the override file sets keys of (an
# override of a missing schema is silently ignored), and the desktop-base
# theme the wallpaper points to.
Depends: gsettings-desktop-schemas,
         gnome-shell,
         desktop-base,
         zyphor-os-artwork,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Zyphor OS defaults for the GNOME desktop
 The look and layout of Zyphor OS's GNOME edition: the desktop-base
 wallpaper and the applications pinned to the dash.
 .
 The settings are a GSettings override (priority 90, above Debian's own), so
 they only change defaults: a user's own choices in dconf always win, and
 Debian's files are left untouched.
